LOGBOOK.md-1343-- FIX (F2, blocking): `ExecRunner` discarded judgeable results through two races on `Host.Call`'s primary path. (a) `return Result{}, writeErr` before stdout was ever considered: an EPIPE racing the plugin's exit threw away valid correlated frames. (b) Found during this rework by driving `Run` directly (2 of 20 crash-script iters returned `read |0: file already closed`): `Wait` closes `StdoutPipe`/`StderrPipe` read ends after seeing the process exit, racing a drain still in flight — this, not EPIPE, is what misclassified the stdin-draining `exit 3` fixture. Fix per the file's own comments: judge whenever possible (non-empty stdout governs; empty stdout with a known exit classifies the crash through the Result), surface write/close/wait failures only with empty stdout and no known exit, and drain over `os.Pipe` pairs owned by `Run` so no later Close can interrupt a drain. New tests `TestExecRunnerKeepsValidFrameWhenPluginIgnoresStdin` (200 calls, zero discards) and `TestExecRunnerClassifiesCrashExitDeterministically` (50 crash calls, all `plugin exited without a response`): both FAIL on the pre-fix runner (2/200 frames discarded; crash misclassified as `runner reported no result`, each verified by swapping the pre-fix `runner.go` back with sha256-verified restore) and pass post-fix.
