LOGBOOK.md-1561-- FIX: both rows now sweep every registered §15.2 failure status rather than one sample, drawn from the production predicate `axerror.IsFailureExitStatus` through one helper that asserts the count is seventeen, so a predicate that answered false for everything would redden instead of turning each loop into a green test that drove nothing. `TestTheExitStatusEqualityBindsACodeTheRegistryDoesNotCarry` first asserts `CodeRegistered() == false` on the conforming read, so the row cannot quietly stop covering the class it exists for if that code is ever registered.
LOGBOOK.md:1562:- DECISION: the enumerator itself carries a mutant. Narrowing its range to `status <= 20` drops exit 130 out of every loop that draws on it, and the asserted count is what makes that a red rather than a silently smaller sweep. A shared helper that decides how much a sweep covers is a gate, and it is measured like one.
