LOGBOOK.md-1638-- SCOPE: `internal/axerror` (new package, TASK-260830-34elja), Structured Error §15.1-15.3.
LOGBOOK.md-1639-- ROOT CAUSE: the first revision of the detail-redaction gate matched key **substrings** — `token`, `socket`, `credential`, `secret`, `pid`, `named_pipe`, ... — against §16.2's whole exclusion table. Two errors in one rule. It refused `token_count`, `socket_timeout_ms` and `credential_profile`, ordinary diagnostics the pinned document admits, while admitting a secret written under any innocuous name: false-positive surface with no true-positive capability. And it applied §16.2, which governs manifests and bundles generated by `ax`, to §15.1 error **details**, whose declared prohibition is exactly four classes — "No detail may contain a credential, raw transcript, environment secret, or opaque bundle content". A detail key naming a PID, a tmux socket or a Terminal Instance Binding is none of those four; refusing it invented a constraint.
LOGBOOK.md:1640:- FINDING: identical shape to BUG-260902-2faftr (`hasForbiddenConfigName`), one section over and one day later, in code written by someone who had not yet read the entry. It survived the whole positive/negative suite and 17 killed mutants, because every test asserted the gate was *reachable* and none asked which pinned line *declared* it. Nothing about mutation score detects an invented constraint: a mutant that deletes an unlicensed refusal correctly reddens the test that pins the unlicensed refusal.
LOGBOOK.md:1641:- FIX: exact-match only, scoped to §15.1's four classes, 27 keys, each row carrying the class it names. `details.go:refuseExcludedKey`. The admitted rows in `TestDetailsRefuseExcludedClasses` are now the load-bearing half: `token_count`, `socket_timeout_ms`, `credential_profile`, `api_key_id`, `pid`, `tmux_socket_path`, `terminal_instance_binding`. A mutant restoring substring matching reddens on those and on nothing else.
LOGBOOK.md:1642:- FINDING: **the registry was its own oracle.** The first version of that test ranged over the production `excludedDetailKeys` map, so the mutant that deletes `password` also deletes its own test case — SURVIVED, at exit 0, with 19 of 20 other mutants killed around it. Fixed by pinning the 27 rows as a reviewed literal table compared against production, the same shape `TestExitStatusRegistryIsClosed` already used for §15.2. General: a table-driven test that iterates the table it is testing measures nothing about the table's contents.
LOGBOOK.md-1643-- FINDING: `exit_code` declared as `*json.Number` admits the JSON **string** `"9"` — `encoding/json` will unmarshal a quoted value into a `json.Number`. A peer could have written its exit status as text and been believed. Now decoded from `json.RawMessage` with a leading-quote refusal, so the JSON type is part of the check. Found by a negative row written to raise branch coverage, not by design review.
LOGBOOK.md-1644-- DECISION: retryability is a refusal table and never a permission. `RetryabilityRefusal` reports only where the pinned document forbids `retryable = true` — exit classes 7, 16, 130 and the codes `operation_uncertain`, `terminal_backend_stale_generation`, `transaction_unknown` — each quoting the sentence that disqualifies it. It never reports that a retry is safe. The complement is not evidence.
LOGBOOK.md-1645-- DECISION: `LocalFromUntrusted` refuses the Directory Node surface. §15.3 leaves its local code as `incompatible_protocol` or `adapter_protocol_violation`/`transport_failure` "as applicable" without fixing which, so the mapping is reported unknown rather than guessed into a literal that would then look normative.
LOGBOOK.md-1646-- DECISION: §17.2 was **not** re-bound to this package despite being named in the task scope. Its single scanner-visible clause is an unknown-**event** reader obligation; an unknown error **code** is not an unknown session event. Its existing wrong binding to `internal/config/writer.go:EncodeCurrent` is left in place and left disclosed rather than rebound to a friendlier symbol.
LOGBOOK.md:1647:- EVIDENCE: §15.1 6/7 and §15.3 2/3, both `partial` and both still refused by assigned-scope admission; §15.2 stays `unmeasured`. Repository `clauses_discharged` 2/394 → 10/394, `acceptance_cases` 43 → 53. Package coverage 99.7%. 20 mutants, each verified present before measurement, 20 killed, harness aborts if a restore leaves the baseline red.
