LOGBOOK.md-2143-- ROOT CAUSE: `internal/localstore/projection_refusal_inventory_test.go` derived expected refusal sites from the production AST but matched only `*ast.Ident` calls named `projectionRefusal`. Six live clauses written as bare `fmt.Errorf("%w: ...", ErrUnsafeOwnership)` or as delegated `verifyOwnerFileInfo`/`verifyOwnerDirectory` guards were invisible to the gate whose job was to notice them, and shipped unpinned while 20+ funnelled sites were enforced.
LOGBOOK.md-2144-- FINDING: A completeness gate over a *pattern* must also police the pattern. Deriving the expected set is not enough if the extraction rule silently excludes a whole syntactic class.
LOGBOOK.md-2145-- FIX: Second funnel `projectionOwnershipRefusal` (`internal/localstore/projection.go:117`) keeps the refusal decision at its call site while preserving the owner-only cause; every projection refusal rerouted through a funnel. Gate now derives two properties — funnel sites need an exercised negative path beneath `openProjection`, AND no projection-owned source may raise a refusal outside a funnel. Build-context filtering added so a platform-specific refusal is not demanded from a platform that cannot run it.
LOGBOOK.md:2146:- ANOMALY: I reproduced the identical bug class inside the fix. The new unrouted check sat behind `typed.Fun.(*ast.Ident)`, and `fmt.Errorf` is a `*ast.SelectorExpr`, so the exact class stayed invisible in code written specifically to catch it. First run of mutant m41 exited 0. Reading the new gate would not have found this; only the behaviour-preserving mutant did.
LOGBOOK.md-2147-- DECISION: Assume "unreachable" last, not first. One clause presumed unreachable — the non-regular branch of `ensureProjectionFileModes` — is drivable through the real production entry by replacing a sidecar with a FIFO in the post-rebuild hook. Only three clauses are genuine TOCTOU re-checks, each annotated with the earlier check that owns the reachable case.
