-- FIX: policy validity is still refused as `invalid_arguments` before direction; only the `fencing_grant_expired` result is deferred. A remote winner therefore returns the existing `remote_owner` park with `not_owner`, making the v0.7.0 §4.2 step-4 attach/takeover path reachable. A local lapsed grant remains `lease_conflict`.
-- EVIDENCE: `TestAuthorizeRemoteInteractiveOwnerLapsedGrantUsesRemoteOfferArm` drives `Authorize` directly; `TestDecideLapsedRemoteOwnerOffersOrParksByInteractiveContext` drives `axpane.Decide` and records `attach_remote`, `takeover_offer`, and noninteractive `parked`. Neighbours are live local grant → authorized, remote noninteractive owner → `remote_owner`, local lapsed grant → `lease_conflict`; remote invalid policy → `invalid_arguments`.
-- SUITE DIFF: fencing baseline 310 PASS per-test rows; final 316 PASS rows. The normalized diff contains only six new named rows (the five arm/neighbor tests plus the remote-invalid-policy preservation test); no existing input moved across a refusal arm.
-- MUTATION: final harness `mutants-full-v3` reports 31 narrowing `N-` rows + one token-preserving `T-census-alias` KILLED, `C-harmless-comment` SURVIVED, `C-not-applied` NOT_APPLIED, and `C-compile-failure` classified with exit 1. The labelled `N-arm-order-expiry-before-direction` row kills the direct regression. No `__pycache__`/`.pyc` artifacts.
-- VALIDATION: final configured commands 1–30 passed with exit 0, including `go test ./... -v -count=1`, race `-timeout 25m`, coverage, 17 fuzz lanes, tracecheck, catalog check, Linux/Windows builds, Windows vet, JSON parsing, board validation, and `git diff --check`. The first post-fix full/race attempt correctly failed only because `internal/terminstance/fencing_grantless_test.go` still asserted the old expiry-first outcome; the updated integration expectations were then rerun green. Relevant final package run: `internal/fencing`, `internal/axpane`, `internal/terminstance` all exit 0; fencing coverage 97.9%.
