-- F1: the grant-precondition class is exactly four members (no grant, no clock reading, lapsed grant, unusable policy) because those are all four refusals `Authorize` can surface after the ownership arms pass — the verdict decides the tuple fact for all four uniformly by never consulting grant/clock/policy, so completeness is structural, not enumerated, and the relative question needs no fallback (same grant facts, and the grant arms do not read `LocalHostID`).
+- F1 (historical rev4 wording): the grant-precondition class is exactly four members (no grant, no clock reading, lapsed grant, unusable policy) because those are all four refusals `Authorize` can surface after the ownership arms pass — the verdict decides the tuple fact without grant/clock/policy. The current BUG-260917-2fwf8e entry above supersedes the old "relative question needs no fallback" sentence for lapsed remote grants: once ownership direction precedes expiry, that relative question can stop at deferred expiry and needs the explicit composition fallback.
 - F2: a narrowing row that spans a definition and its use is one plant, not two — the E3 row captures the entry instant and passes it to the in-loop authorization check, and either half alone breaks the build, so the kill measures the pair (same precedent as the rev3 resumption row spanning two adjacent checks).
 - F3: a grammar arm masked by a downstream arm is unmeasurable alone — the verdict's presented-session grammar arm needed the agreed-malformed member (both sides naming one malformed session, so only the grammar arm undecides it) because any other malformed session mismatches first.
 - MUTATION EVIDENCE: 114 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 116/116 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after/across. The eleven verdict rows mutate the landed package and are killed through `ObserveFencing`, so the composition — not the helper — is measured. The five surviving rev3 reviewer narrowings (RV3-M1/M2/M3/M4/M8) are mirrored as committed rows with committed killers; RV3-M6/M7 were already killed by the committed suite. Retired `N-fencing-epoch-only` (provably equivalent post-fix: a stale park implies a decided-stale verdict and both arms call `fenceLive` with the same refusal) and re-keyed `N-fencing-operation` to the non-live killer (launch-class now shows on the surfaced park vocabulary). No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.
