+- F1 (historical rev4 wording): the grant-precondition class is exactly four members (no grant, no clock reading, lapsed grant, unusable policy) because those are all four refusals `Authorize` can surface after the ownership arms pass — the verdict decides the tuple fact without grant/clock/policy. The current BUG-260917-2fwf8e entry above supersedes the old "relative question needs no fallback" sentence for lapsed remote grants: once ownership direction precedes expiry, that relative question can stop at deferred expiry and needs the explicit composition fallback.
