 - MUTATION EVIDENCE: 114 narrowing mutants plus one tightening edge row, all KILLED (`mutant_harness.py`, 116/116 with the harmless SURVIVED control on two full passes, verdict lists identical), per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits on both passes, production blobs byte-identical before/after/across. The eleven verdict rows mutate the landed package and are killed through `ObserveFencing`, so the composition — not the helper — is measured. The five surviving rev3 reviewer narrowings (RV3-M1/M2/M3/M4/M8) are mirrored as committed rows with committed killers; RV3-M6/M7 were already killed by the committed suite. Retired `N-fencing-epoch-only` (provably equivalent post-fix: a stale park implies a decided-stale verdict and both arms call `fenceLive` with the same refusal) and re-keyed `N-fencing-operation` to the non-live killer (launch-class now shows on the surfaced park vocabulary). No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.
